Prevent GAMESS rungms from hanging after successful calculations under Slurm.
The final `srun rm -rf "$SCR"` starts another Slurm job step that can remain
pending indefinitely even when GAMESS has terminated normally. Skip this step
and leave scratch cleanup to the caller or site-specific job cleanup. This also
preserves the temporary scratch directory used by EasyBuild regression tests.

Author: Pavel Tomanek (Inuits/UGent) with help from ChatGPT6.0
--- a/rungms-dev
+++ b/rungms-dev
@@ -1756,7 +1756,7 @@
      # Don't use srun for removing directories on a shared file system (e.g., Orion)
      rm -rf "$SCR"
   else
-     srun rm -rf "$SCR"
+     echo "Skipping Slurm scratch cleanup"
   endif
 endif
 #--use-with-care rm -v "$SCR/"*
